module github.com/simple-container-com/sc-component-backup/service

// Bumped from 1.26.11 for go-embedb (see `replace` below), which
// pins `go 1.27.3` in its module directive.
go 1.27.3

// go-embedb is a private fork identified by the upstream FerretDB
// module path, so it has to be routed with a `replace`. It MUST be a
// module path and a pseudo-version, never a filesystem path: a
// sibling-path replace (`../../go-embedb`) resolves only on an operator
// box that happens to have the fork checked out, and it fails in
// `go mod download` — i.e. while loading the module graph, before any
// build tag or env var is read. That is how 3a888c5 took this repo's
// `main` red with the USE_GOEMBEDB flag still defaulted off: the flag
// cannot gate a dependency the module graph needs to resolve.
//
// A filesystem replace also never validates the pseudo-version string,
// which hid a second defect in that commit — its timestamp
// (20261123155907) is not the commit's (20261123133627).
//
// The repo is PRIVATE, so CI needs credentials to fetch it. They come
// from this repo's own SC registry (`.sc/secrets.yaml`, decrypted with
// the single org-level SC_CONFIG) and reach the Docker build as a
// buildx secret mount — see service/Dockerfile and README.md §Storage.
replace github.com/FerretDB/FerretDB => github.com/simple-container-com/go-embedb v0.0.0-20261124214336-b3607f5d06ea

